// Neko — a pixel-art cat living on the desktop.
// @channels bufferA, tex1
// @sim-max-height 128
//
// After the classic oneko. The cat chases the cursor, leaping onto the top
// of the window under it, and sits beside it; while the cursor rests it
// washes, scratches, yawns and curls up asleep, and moving the cursor wakes
// it with a start. Left alone it lives its own life: walks the window tops,
// naps on them, peeks out from behind a window's edge, and now and then taps
// a mug or a pencil off a window top to watch it fall. A dragged window
// carries it along until it jumps off and twists upright in the air.
// Hover slowly over the cat to pet it (it purrs); click it for a meow; click
// bare desktop to throw it a ball of yarn. By the local clock it sleeps in a
// basket by a lamp at night and asks for food at breakfast and dinner.
//
// iChannel0  Buffer A: the cat, the yarn ball and the falling object (layout
//            in neko_common.frag).
// iChannel1  Wallpaper ("Image 2" in the settings), cover-fitted behind the
//            cat. Without one a warm room wall and a wooden floor are drawn.
//
// The cat is 32 x 32 pixel art, 4 bits per pixel, drawn at a whole number of
// screen pixels per sprite pixel (1/340 of the shorter screen side at cat
// size 1); props and furniture share that pixel grid.

